 diagonal matrix. It's a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. But some of the entries that do not lie on the main diagonal are not zeros (for instance, ${y}_{31}=1\\ne 0$).\n\nTherefore, only $S$ is a diagonal matrix."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186568918 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a117d47f-5218-5d82-82e9-ffcf370c0559" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569004} {:answer/id #uuid "bf860344-eec5-56e2-88c2-3d436b9ef657" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf860344-eec5-56e2-88c2-3d436b9ef657" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569022} :answer-field/id #uuid "0918ebc1-241e-57b0-a7b8-ffeaf8e948af" :answer-field/key "M" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186568903} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dfe29f00-601a-59c2-b837-432d3e7573a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569046} {:answer/id #uuid "e466fa8c-ff2c-5668-8138-7a890709c54c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569051}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfe29f00-601a-59c2-b837-432d3e7573a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569046} :answer-field/id #uuid "421d3f3c-f9a3-5633-b85b-c6827c768ae0" :answer-field/key "N" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186568939} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "542877b5-2124-56a5-9ccc-0c4493e4b1a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186568950} {:answer/id #uuid "ba191f7c-41a8-599a-a64b-3192adaf21d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba191f7c-41a8-599a-a64b-3192adaf21d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569020} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3f56e11-5cae-56d8-a7af-b22ae9dce269" :answer-field/key "P" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569037}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1cbde6d3-f61c-55c1-811a-ce46bfabb978" :question/problem "Which of the following are identity matrices?\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$M=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$N=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- $M$ is *not* an identity matrix. It is not a square matrix: it has 2 rows and 3 columns.\n\n- $N$ is an identity matrix. It is square, every main diagonal entry is one, and every off-diagonal entry is zero.\n\n- $P$ is an identity matrix. It is square, every main diagonal entry is one, and every off-diagonal entry is zero.\n\nTherefore, only $N$ and $P$ are identity matrices."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186568922 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08ef2289-f91e-51ed-963f-d0c4cdf85c7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186568902} {:answer/id #uuid "cac55895-5084-5d25-aa5a-af919b6b7400" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cac55895-5084-5d25-aa5a-af919b6b7400" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569030} :answer-field/id #uuid "1630bab9-0849-50f8-b5ac-d394dc1848ec" :answer-field/key "M" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186568916} {:answer-field/choices [{