rix. It is square, but an entry off the main diagonal is nonzero: ${p}_{32}=7\\ne 0$.\n\nTherefore, only $M$ is an identity matrix."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186569057 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "776ccc75-5cc1-5878-853d-7b45c9c88c40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186568976} {:answer/id #uuid "e1bb5d36-cebd-5fcb-9aed-9834e0f727b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "776ccc75-5cc1-5878-853d-7b45c9c88c40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186568976} :answer-field/id #uuid "99f87280-7599-5091-b2a4-dffb118936f9" :answer-field/key "F" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186568999} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a198d32-5a2d-5ca0-b73e-32caa9decf80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569000} {:answer/id #uuid "da09a4d6-05c5-54f3-a8d4-4a0303b3c97a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da09a4d6-05c5-54f3-a8d4-4a0303b3c97a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569041} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2137564-01a9-5542-8936-647ede6382ea" :answer-field/key "H" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569005} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a7b9399-6f0f-57a2-96a3-ff3cfea206d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186568935} {:answer/id #uuid "e4f0b1aa-bb0b-5a3f-a707-9620fc78429a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a7b9399-6f0f-57a2-96a3-ff3cfea206d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186568935} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4c0c1a8-d7dd-5320-b757-95ffbad65c55" :answer-field/key "M" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569052}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f8362953-d427-5947-9c92-d04953c2223a" :question/problem "Which of the following are diagonal matrices?\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$F=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$H=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$M=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- $F$ is a diagonal matrix. It is square and every off-diagonal entry is zero. It is also an identity matrix; identity matrices are diagonal matrices.\n\n- $H$ is *not* a diagonal matrix. It is square, but an entry off the main diagonal is nonzero: ${h}_{12}=1\\ne 0$.\n\n- $M$ is a diagonal matrix. It is square and every off-diagonal entry is zero. It is also an identity matrix; identity matrices are diagonal matrices.\n\nTherefore, only $F$ and $M$ are diagonal matrices."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Special Square Matrix"}]}
